<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janusz III of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1502–1526</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Janusz III was the last Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a>, ruling jointly with his elder brother Stanisław. Both brothers died young, Stanisław in 1524 and Janusz in 1526, amid rumours of poisoning. Their deaths ended the Masovian Piast line, and King Sigismund I incorporated Masovia into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> later became the royal capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janusz-iii-of-masovia.jpg" alt="Janusz III of Masovia" width="277" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Masovia)Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janusz_Mazowiecki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
